+---
+type: spec
+task_slug: parse-iso-duration
+status: approved
+created: 2026-10-15
+tags: [timeparse, spec, python, iso-8601, duration-parsing]
+test_framework: pytest
+interview_rounds: 0
+lane: light
+summary: "Add parse_iso_duration: day-and-time ISO-8601 durations to seconds, exported from timeparse"
+---
+
+# SPEC: parse_iso_duration
+
+## 🎯 Intent
+`timeparse.parse_duration` only reads the compact `1h30m` style. Callers receiving ISO-8601 durations
+(`PT1H30M`) have no parser. Add one for the day-and-time subset, leaving `parse_duration` untouched.
+
+## 🌅 Outcomes
+`from timeparse import parse_iso_duration` works, and `parse_iso_duration("P1DT2H")` returns `93600`.
+Anything outside the grammar raises `ValueError`.
+
+## 📋 In-Scope Scenarios
+
+### AC-001: Valid durations return seconds
+**Given** text matching `P[nD][T[nH][nM][nS]]` (n = ASCII digits, upper-case designators, optional surrounding whitespace)
+**When** `parse_iso_duration(text)` is called
+**Then** it returns `86400*D + 3600*H + 60*M + S` as an `int`
+**And** values may exceed the next unit (`PT90M` → 5400); `P1D` → 86400, `PT1H30M` → 5400, `P1DT2H` → 93600, `PT0S` → 0
+
+### AC-002: Invalid durations raise ValueError
+**Given** text with no component (`P`, `PT`, `""`), a `T` with no `H`/`M`/`S` (`P1DT`), out-of-order or repeated components (`PT1M1H`, `PT1H1H`),
+Y / W / month-before-`T` (`P1Y`, `P1W`, `P1M`), fractions (`PT1.5S`), signs (`-P1D`, `PT-1S`), lower case (`pt1h`), a missing `P`, a missing number (`PTH`),
+non-ASCII digits (`P١D`), or internal whitespace (`P1D T1H`)
+**When** `parse_iso_duration(text)` is called
+**Then** it raises `ValueError`
+
+### AC-003: Export and no regression
+**Given** the `timeparse` package
+**When** it is imported
+**Then** `parse_iso_duration` is importable from `timeparse` and listed in `__all__`
+**And** `parse_duration` behaves exactly as before (existing `tests/test_parse.py` passes unchanged)
+
+## 🚫 Non-Goals
+- Years, months, weeks, fractions, signs, lower case, `PnDTnH` alternative/extended formats.
+- Any change to `parse_duration`, `UNITS`, `format_duration` or the CLI.
+- Non-`str` inputs (behaviour unspecified).
+
+## ⚠️ Constraints
+| Constraint | Value | Rationale |
+|---|---|---|
+| Test framework | `pytest` | Existing `tests/test_parse.py` uses it |
+| Implementation | stdlib only, in `timeparse/parse.py` | Ask names the file; no new dependency |
+| Digits | ASCII `0-9` only | `\d` would accept Unicode digits that `int()` converts; the grammar says integers |
+| Compatibility | existing Python range in `pyproject.toml` | No new syntax |
+
+## 🔒 Irreversible Decisions
+none — the name and signature are fixed by the ask; adding a function is cheaply revertible.
+
+## ✅ Verification Criteria
+| Scenario | Verification mode | Test name / manual step |
+|---|---|---|
+| AC-001 | unit | `test_iso_valid` (parametrized golden table) |
+| AC-002 | unit | `test_iso_invalid` (parametrized) |
+| AC-003 | unit | `test_iso_exported`; existing `tests/test_parse.py` |
+
+## ❓ Open Questions
+None.
+
+## 🔍 Refinement Decisions
+- Not skipped by Step 0: new public function (contract change). Lane `light`: 2 source files, one session, no irreversible decision.
+- Interview skipped (0 rounds): the ask fixes grammar, examples and failures; no WHAT ambiguity. Autopilot `auto_full` armed, so no question was put to the DRI.
+- Defaulted: ASCII-only digits, internal whitespace invalid, `P0D` valid (0), surrounding whitespace stripped via `str.strip()`.
+- Oracle: golden for AC-001/002, sourced from the user-supplied examples and ISO-8601 unit arithmetic (1d=86400, 1h=3600, 1m=60); edge inputs in AC-002 are derived from the stated grammar rules.
